  "title": "The diminished triad",
  "summary": "Two minor 3rds stacked: a tense, unstable chord.",
  "minutes": 5,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Diminished triad",
      "body": "Stack two minor 3rds and you get a **diminished triad**: root, minor 3rd, and a tritone (6 half steps) above the root. B diminished is B D F. Its chord symbol is **Bdim** or **B°**.\n\n**Why it matters:** It is the only triad on the white keys that is neither major nor minor (B D F), and its tension pulls strongly to the next chord. You will see it often in Unit 5.",
